Ladybird resolves a MediaMetadata’s artwork URLs against the base URL
of the current settings object, as Blink and WebKit do: Blink completes
them with ExecutionContext::From(script_state) in media_session_utils,
and WebKit parses them with the ScriptExecutionContext its IDL passes as
CurrentScriptExecutionContext. Gecko follows the spec text instead, and
resolves them against GetEntryDocument()’s base URI.
